      "decision": "Effective-state helper: timestamp-driven lazy activation (D4). Add nullable scheduled_start_at / scheduled_end_at columns to app.examinations and introduce ONE authoritative helper, ExaminationEffectiveState(exam) -> {phase: 'inactive'|'active'|'ended', activeNow bool}, consulted by the activation gate, the submission gate, the questions gate, and the SSE push. effective active = is_active=true AND (scheduled_start_at IS NULL OR now()>=scheduled_start_at) AND (scheduled_end_at IS NULL OR now()<scheduled_end_at). 'Instant activate' = set is_active=true, activated_at=now(), scheduled_start_at=now(), scheduled_end_at=NULL. 'Activate at time, limited window' = is_active=true, scheduled_start_at=T0, scheduled_end_at=T1 (sandbox NOT cloned yet). 'Deactivate at time' = set scheduled_end_at=T1 (the lazy gate stops accepting submissions at T1 even though is_active stays true until a real deactivate drops the sandbox). 'Instant deactivate' = existing Phase 3 ArchiveExamination (is_active=false, archived_at=now(), drop sandbox). Lazy sandbox prep: on the FIRST request inside the active window that needs the sandbox (first DML submission OR first GetExamQuestions that detects examHasDMLQuestions), call InitializeExamSandbox(examID) guarded by app.exam_sandboxes (created_at IS NOT NULL, dropped_at IS NULL) so it clones at most once; InitializeExamSandbox is already idempotent. The activation PRE-FLIGHT (every question expected_result_status='captured') still runs at the moment is_active is flipped to true, regardless of scheduled_start_at, so a scheduled exam cannot be armed with uncaptured questions.",
      "rationale": "D4 mandates no background scheduler/cron. A single pure helper computing effective state from now() vs timestamps at request time keeps all four gates consistent and avoids split-brain between a boolean and a clock. Reusing is_active as the 'armed' flag and scheduled_* as the window keeps the existing freeze logic (UpsertQuestion/ImportSchema/AssignStudents check is_active) working unchanged. Lazy sandbox prep honors the constraint that pure-SELECT exams never clone and that DML exams must have a sandbox ready on first access, without a scheduler.",
