      "id": "ARCH-002",
      "decision": "SSE realtime activation push (D2, R10) \u2014 the infrastructure R9 depends on. Add a new authenticated SSE endpoint GET /api/v1/quiz/exams/:id/stream that holds an HTTP connection open and pushes a single 'exam-status' event whenever the exam's effective state (ARCH-001) transitions to active for an enrolled student. Server model: an in-process pub/sub hub (services/sse_hub.go) keyed by examID, holding a set of subscriber channels. gin handler: authenticate (see token note), verify enrollment, set headers (Content-Type: text/event-stream, Cache-Control: no-cache, Connection: keep-alive, X-Accel-Buffering: no), register a buffered channel with the hub, then loop with c.Stream / Flush emitting: (a) an immediate snapshot event computed from ExaminationEffectiveState so a client connecting AFTER activation is told 'active' at once (no race), (b) periodic ':keepalive' comments every ~20s to defeat idle proxies, (c) the 'start' event when the hub broadcasts activation. Each event carries id: <unix-ms> for Last-Event-ID. Activation trigger: ActivateExamination (instant) and the lazy gate that first observes now()>=scheduled_start_at both call hub.Broadcast(examID, statusEvent). Because scheduled activation has no background tick, the snapshot-on-connect plus a client-side fallback poll (ARCH-009) covers the gap where the window opens while a student waits with an already-open stream \u2014 the lazy trigger fires on the first enrolled student's poll/stream-reconnect, which then broadcasts to all held connections. Reconnection: EventSource auto-reconnects; server reads Last-Event-ID but state is idempotent (re-sends current snapshot), so no event log is needed. Graceful shutdown: hub closes all channels on SIGTERM (tolerant-of-restarts per constraints; clients auto-reconnect).",
      "rationale": "D2 locks SSE. SSE removes polling for a one-way server->client 'start' signal, needs no extra infra (no Redis/Kafka), and a single Go process trivially holds 90-150 idle held connections (goroutine + channel each). WebSocket REJECTED: bidirectional, needs Upgrade handshake + nginx proxy upgrade plumbing the current config explicitly strips, and we only need one-way push. Nginx LB REJECTED: only spreads polling load, never removes the poll; SSE eliminates it. Snapshot-on-connect eliminates the activation/connection race that a naive broadcast-only design would have.",
